{
  "_about": "Draft level layouts for the Comfy office demo, built from the photos in new-office and old-office. Tile coordinates are [col, row], origin top-left of the grid, 2:1 isometric, tile 128x64. Rooms are rectangles [col, row, width, depth]. Walls are drawn on the north and west edges of each room, which are the two edges visible in isometric view. Every object names a generated asset; footprint is [width, depth] in tiles. This is a starting point for the map painter, not a final map. Walls: north and west edges are back walls, south and east edges are low near-side stubs. wall_variants swap in a wall texture with a window or door drawn on it. doorways are tiles with no wall so rooms connect. wall_overrides set a stretch of wall to glass. Indexes (at) count tiles along that edge from the room's first column or row.",
